{
  "summary": "Removes echoing of raw input strings and key material in error messages emitted during descriptor parsing, wallet imports, and transaction funding. Replaces echoed inputs with descriptor indices or public representations via ToString(), identifies failing keys in multi-key expressions by positional index, and restricts quoted function names to a predefined allowlist of known descriptor functions. Updates functional and unit tests to verify sanitized error messages and assert that secret key material is never reflected.",
  "problem": "Descriptors supplied to RPC methods can contain private keys such as WIF strings or extended private keys (xprvs). When parsing or derivation fails, existing error messages echo the input string, key path values, or checksums, leaking sensitive private key material into application logs, exception reporting systems, or support screenshots.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Some descriptor error messages quote the string the caller sent, and a descriptor can hold a private key. The error then carries the key, or part of it, into places the request may not go: an application's log, an error reporter, a screenshot shared for help.'",
    "Commit 5f1576be35: 'Several error messages quote text from the descriptor the caller sent, and that text can be a private key. Error text is often logged or shared where the request is not. Even the first characters of a key give away part of it.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Replaced the previous approach of capping echoed token lengths with an allowlist of known descriptor function names and complete suppression of raw key or path value strings. Added positional key indexing for multi-key expressions (multi, musig, miniscript) and array indexing for descriptor inputs.",
  "card": "Stops descriptor parsing and wallet RPC errors from echoing raw key material back to callers. Descriptors can contain private keys (WIF, xprv), and syntax or derivation errors previously reflected the raw input strings or fragments into error messages, risking exposure in application logs, error monitoring tools, or user screenshots. The change suppresses echoing raw key strings, indexes keys within multi-key expressions by position, restricts quoted function names to a static allowlist, and emits public descriptor representations (desc->ToString()) where available. Tests are added across functional test suites to ensure private key substrings never leak into error messages.",
